  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 149 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nIt's a very nice end to the weekend with clear skies and \ntemperatures in the 60s areawide. We'll continue to warm up \nthroughout the afternoon as gusty winds mix down warmer air \njust above the surface. This quiet and warm weather pattern will\ncontinue for the majority of the week as high pressure dominates \nthe central US. \n\nIt will be interesting to track our average temperature\nthroughout the month as this abnormally warm weather \ncontinues. Even with our recent cooldown, MSP is on track to be \nthe warmest October on record. As of Oct 17th, our average \ntemperature this month has been 59.3F and the all time monthly \nrecord is 59.2F from 1947. For St Cloud, the record is 58.2F \n(1900) and it is at 54.3F through Oct 17th. For Eau Claire, the \nrecord is 59.2F (1947) and it is at 56.1F through Oct 17th.\n\nBy this weekend, a longwave trough is expected to track over \nthe western US and produce a couple chances for rain as is moves\neastward. Amounts in our area continue to look unimpressive and\nthe latest NBM PoPs peak around 30 to 50 percent on Saturday.",
